    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Each player contributes a stake to the pool. The dealer gives three cards face-down to each player and turns up one card; if it is not lower than an eight (ace lowest), the dealer continues turning up cards until such a card is exposed. The player on the dealer's left, without touching or looking at their three cards, may bet the amount of the pool or any part of it that they hold a card of the same suit higher than the turn-up. If they win they take that amount from the pool; if they lose they pay it to the pool. Each player does the same in turn, the dealer last. When the pool is exhausted a fresh stake is put in. After a round the deal passes. No player may touch any cards until making a bet; the penalty is a fine to the pool of twice the stake and loss of the right to bet that round.",
    Player: "Each player contributes a stake to the pool. The dealer gives three cards face-down to each player and turns up one card; if it is not lower than an eight (ace lowest), the dealer continues turning up cards until such a card is exposed. The player on the dealer's left, without touching or looking at their three cards, may bet the amount of the pool or any part of it that they hold a card of the same suit higher than the turn-up. If they win they take that amount from the pool; if they lose they pay it to the pool. Each player does the same in turn, the dealer last. When the pool is exhausted a fresh stake is put in. After a round the deal passes. No player may touch any cards until making a bet; the penalty is a fine to the pool of twice the stake and loss of the right to bet that round.",
    objective: 'Win chips from the pool by matching the suit of the target card with a higher-ranking card from your hand.',
    gameplay: "Each player contributes a stake to the pool. The dealer gives three cards face-down to each player and turns up one card; if it is not lower than an eight (ace lowest), the dealer continues turning up cards until such a card is exposed. The player on the dealer's left, without touching or looking at their three cards, may bet the amount of the pool or any part of it that they hold a card of the same suit higher than the turn-up. If they win they take that amount from the pool; if they lose they pay it to the pool. Each player does the same in turn, the dealer last. When the pool is exhausted a fresh stake is put in. After a round the deal passes. No player may touch any cards until making a bet; the penalty is a fine to the pool of twice the stake and loss of the right to bet that round.",
    keyRules: [
      'Blind bet: do not look at or touch your three cards before announcing your bet.',
      'Bet up to the full pool or any part of it that you hold a same-suit higher card than the turn-up.',
      'Turn-up must be lower than 8 (ace low); dealer keeps turning until it is.',
      'Touching cards before betting: fine of twice the stake to the pool and loss of bet right for that round.',
